<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stepan Shaumian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1878">1878</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Stepan Shahumyan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stepan Shaumian was an Armenian Bolshevik who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku">Baku</a> Commune, the Soviet government of Baku, in 1918. When the commune fell in July 1918 he and other leaders were arrested; they were shot by anti-Bolshevik forces in the Transcaspian desert in September 1918, remembered in Soviet history as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/26-baku-commissars">26 Baku Commissars</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stepan-shaumian.jpg" alt="Stepan Shaumian" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stepan_Shahumyan_youth.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
